    "result_text": "Done. The change is implemented and the full test suite is green.\n\n## What I did\n\nThe app serves `POST /api/owners` as an OfficeFloor function pipeline. I added a new validation step that rejects a supplied `registrationDate` later than the server's current date with a 400:\n\n1. **`ValidateRegistrationDate`** (`rest/function/owner/`) \u2014 reads the body already published by `ValidateNewOwner` (the HTTP body can only be bound once per pipeline via `@Val OwnerFieldsDto`), and throws `FutureRegistrationDateException` when a supplied date is after `LocalDate.now()`. It's a no-op when no date is supplied, preserving the existing default-to-server-date behavior in `BuildOwner`.\n\n2. **`FutureRegistrationDateException`** (checked, `extends Exception`) + **`FutureRegistrationDateExceptionHandler`** \u2014 responds `400` with `{\"errors\": [\"registrationDate\"]}`, matching the existing field-validation error shape (e.g. `InvalidTelephoneException`).\n\n3. **Escalation YAML** mapping the exception to its handler.\n\n4. **Wired the step** into `owners.POST.yml` between `validate` and `validatePostcode`, so an invalid body is a 400 before any entity is built or persisted.\n\nThe step runs before weekend/business-day adjustment, so it compares the raw supplied date against the server date as the spec requires.\n\n**Results:** `AcceptanceTest.errorRejectsFutureDate` passes, and `./mvnw test` reports `BUILD SUCCESS` (1 test, 0 failures).",
